#set heading(numbering: none)
= Glossary
<glossary>
#strong[Adapter] --- Software that translates an approved system interface into a defined retrieval or calculation contract. An adapter is separate from the database or application it accesses.

#strong[Agent] --- An LLM behavior profile with instructions, tool access, and a defined role in a workflow.

#strong[Artifact] --- A durable output from an engineering workflow, such as a notebook, source manifest, `results.json`, figure, or report.

#strong[Barrier] --- A preventive or mitigating measure that reduces the likelihood or consequence of a hazardous event.

#strong[Binary Interaction Parameter (BIP)] --- A fitted parameter $k_(i j)$ that corrects the geometric mean combining rule for the cross-energy parameter in cubic equations of state.

#strong[CMMS] --- Computerized maintenance management system, used to manage maintenance work, equipment records and related resources.

#strong[Deployment Profile] --- A policy setting that controls which MCP tools and levels of autonomy are appropriate for a desktop, study-team, digital-twin, or enterprise context.

#strong[EAM] --- Enterprise asset management, covering asset information and lifecycle work such as maintenance, inspection and planning.

#strong[Equation of State (EOS)] --- A mathematical relation between pressure, volume, and temperature that describes the thermodynamic state of a fluid.

#strong[Evidence package] --- The reviewed records, extracted values, assumptions and provenance supplied to an engineering study.

#strong[Flash Calculation] --- The computation of phase compositions and amounts at thermodynamic equilibrium for a given feed at specified conditions (e.g., T, P).

#strong[Fugacity] --- An effective partial pressure that accounts for non-ideal behavior. Phases are in equilibrium when component fugacities are equal across all phases.

#strong[GIS] --- Geographic information system, used to manage location-based records such as routes, elevations and spatial asset relationships.

#strong[HAZOP] --- Hazard and Operability study, a structured workshop method for identifying process deviations, causes, consequences, and safeguards.

#strong[Historian] --- A time-series database for plant operating measurements, including timestamps and quality information.

#strong[HSE] --- Health, safety, and environment; the organizational and engineering functions concerned with protecting people, assets, and the environment.

#strong[LIMS] --- Laboratory information management system, used to manage samples, analyses, results and laboratory approval status.

#strong[LLM] --- Large language model; the reasoning and language interface that can plan steps, call tools, and write explanations.

#strong[LOPA] --- Layer of Protection Analysis, a semi-quantitative method for evaluating whether independent protection layers reduce scenario risk sufficiently.

#strong[MCP] --- Model Context Protocol, a protocol that lets LLM clients discover and invoke external tools and resources through structured messages.

#strong[Memory] --- Stored user, repository, or session knowledge that helps an agent reuse verified facts and avoid repeated mistakes.

#strong[Mixing Rule] --- The prescription for combining pure-component EOS parameters into mixture parameters.

#strong[MOC] --- Management of change, the organization's controlled process for assessing, approving, implementing and recording changes.

#strong[NeqSim] --- Non-Equilibrium Simulator. An open-source Java toolkit for thermodynamic calculations and process simulation.

#strong[ProcessModel] --- A NeqSim model that composes multiple named process areas, each often represented by a `ProcessSystem`.

#strong[ProcessSystem] --- A NeqSim flowsheet containing streams, equipment, controllers, and process connections for one process area.

#strong[Professional Ladder] --- Discipline career and authority structure responsible for maintaining professional quality, methods, mentoring, and technical standards within an engineering domain.

#strong[Provenance] --- Traceable information about where a value or result came from, including source, revision, retrieval time, method, and review status.

#strong[Reference conditions] --- The stated temperature and pressure, and any other relevant basis, used to express a volume or flow. Standard volume is incomplete without its reference convention.

#strong[SAP] --- Enterprise resource planning system commonly used for equipment master data, maintenance notifications, work orders, and spare-parts context.

#strong[Scenario] --- A named set of model inputs, operating assumptions and constraints whose results are evaluated together.

#strong[SIL] --- Safety Integrity Level, a target reliability classification for safety instrumented functions.

#strong[Skill] --- A curated knowledge package that teaches an agent when and how to perform a domain task.

#strong[Source Manifest] --- A structured list of documents, tags, database records, and assumptions used in a study.

#strong[Technical Safety] --- Engineering discipline focused on preventing, controlling, and mitigating major accident risk through barriers, safety studies, standards, and lifecycle assurance.

#strong[Tool] --- A callable function outside the language model, such as an MCP calculation, file reader, document retriever, or historian query.

#strong[Trivial equilibrium solution] --- A numerical result in which the supposed coexisting phases have the same composition and properties. It requires further physical checks before being accepted as a phase boundary.


#set heading(numbering: none)
= About the Author
<about-the-author>
Even Solbraa is a professor in process engineering and the original creator of NeqSim, a Java library for thermodynamic calculations and process simulation. His work has focused on applying rigorous thermodynamics, process modelling, and digital engineering workflows to oil and gas production, gas processing, CCS, and field development studies. This book reflects the ongoing effort to connect NeqSim with modern agentic engineering workflows, including MCP tools, AI coding agents, technical document retrieval, plant historian data, and reproducible engineering reports.


